From f8c8df27e4a729b99c2f0ebf7c517a39fb6a3861 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tigerblue77 <37409593+tigerblue77@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:03:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] RIG ONLY: carry the real-time class to ublk as REQ_META

Not for upstream and never for a real disk.  The host-like I/O rig
emulates SATA disks with hddsim, a ublk server.  ublk passes a
request's FAILFAST, META, FUA, NOUNMAP, SWAP and INTEGRITY flags to
its server but not its I/O priority (ublk_setup_iod(), Linux 7.0), so
hddsim cannot see the real-time class zfs_vdev_disk_rt_mask gives
synchronous I/O.  Mark those bios REQ_META, which ublk passes as
UBLK_IO_F_META and hddsim reads as the NCQ high-priority bit.

Only reads and the writes blk-wbt leaves alone (REQ_SYNC and REQ_IDLE,
which zfs_vdev_disk_sync_writes sets where that parameter exists) are
marked: blk-wbt gives a REQ_META write its highest limit, which would
mix a blk-wbt effect into the NCQ one.  On the rig nothing else reads
REQ_META: the scheduler is none and no blk-cgroup I/O controller is
enabled.

Signed-off-by: Tigerblue77 <37409593+tigerblue77@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 module/os/linux/zfs/vdev_disk.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/module/os/linux/zfs/vdev_disk.c b/module/os/linux/zfs/vdev_disk.c
index cf4ebd393cf..2bdaa26269b 100644
--- a/module/os/linux/zfs/vdev_disk.c
+++ b/module/os/linux/zfs/vdev_disk.c
@@ -847,6 +847,20 @@ vbio_add_page(vbio_t *vbio, struct page *page, uint_t size, uint_t offset)
 			    WRITE : READ, vbio->vbio_flags);
 			bio->bi_ioprio = vbio->vbio_ioprio;
 
+			/*
+			 * Test rig only, never for a real disk: ublk does not
+			 * pass a request's I/O priority to its server, so
+			 * carry the real-time class to the hddsim emulator as
+			 * REQ_META.  Not on a write blk-wbt throttles, whose
+			 * limit REQ_META would raise.
+			 */
+			if (IOPRIO_PRIO_CLASS(vbio->vbio_ioprio) ==
+			    IOPRIO_CLASS_RT &&
+			    (vbio->vbio_zio->io_type == ZIO_TYPE_READ ||
+			    (vbio->vbio_flags & (REQ_SYNC | REQ_IDLE)) ==
+			    (REQ_SYNC | REQ_IDLE)))
+				bio->bi_opf |= REQ_META;
+
 			if (vbio->vbio_bio) {
 				bio_chain(vbio->vbio_bio, bio);
 				vdev_submit_bio(vbio->vbio_bio);
